WEBVTT


00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:03.959
Dad, what's happening?


00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:06.364
Nick, listen to me like we're


00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:08.764
the last two people on
the planet. Okay? Nick,


00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:13.035
Some day a girl is going
to give you a flower.


00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:15.372
You got that? A flower.


00:01:15.442 --> 00:01:16.966
And you have to help her.


00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:19.011
You help her and
you help us all.


00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.104
Okay?


00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.810
I know it doesn't make
any sense right now,


00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:27.045
but I believe the
woman who told me that.


00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:29.483
You think you
could believe me?


00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:33.049
I love you.


00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.721
I always said you
were special, Nick.


00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:41.323
Turns out I was right.


00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:53.240
Division's here.
Just keep moving.


00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:56.043
And don't make any decisions
that any watcher can track.


00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:42.061
I just wanted to
have a conversation.


00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:05.874
What a waste.


00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.147
Bring his body to the lab.


00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:17.487
There are special
people in this world.


00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:20.029
We don't ask to be special.


00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:22.296
We're just born this way.


00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:29.206
We pass you on the
streets every day,


00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:31.974
unnoticed by most.


00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:43.546
It started in 1945.


00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:47.489
The Nazis were conducting
experiments in psychic warfare...


00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:51.755
trying to turn those with
psychic abilities into soldiers.


00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:55.323
Lots of us died.


00:03:55.435 --> 00:03:56.663
The war ended,


00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:58.938
but the experiments
never stopped.


00:03:59.606 --> 00:04:01.267
Other governments
around the world


00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:03.671
set up what they
called "Divisions"...


00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:09.211
trying to do what
the Nazis couldn't,


00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:10.907
to turn us into weapons.


00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:15.247
Division's agents are trained to
track and hunt us down like animals...


00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:17.687
take us away from our
families and friends.


00:04:18.625 --> 00:04:21.321
There are children stuffed
away all over the world.


00:04:21.561 --> 00:04:23.961
They test us and
categorize us.


00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:26.095
I'm what they
call a "watcher".


00:04:26.232 --> 00:04:27.494
We can see the future,


00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:29.694
even if that's not always
as simple as it sounds.


00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:33.637
The jumbo jet crashed. There
are no reports of survivors.


00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:35.196
Others are called "movers",


00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:37.702
just an easy way of
saying "telekinetic".


00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:44.849
"Pushers" put
thoughts in your head


00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:47.283
and make whatever lie they
come up with the truth.


00:04:47.387 --> 00:04:49.878
They'd already begun
to control my mind...


00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:57.493
"Sniffs",
"shifters", "shadows",


00:04:57.563 --> 00:05:00.031
"bleeders", it goes on and on.


00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:03.667
In Division's eyes,
we're all just lab rats.


00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:08.273
Only one problem:
we keep dying.


00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:12.435
The evidence shows that the kids were
given milk with radioactive iodine.


00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:15.777
No one has ever survived the
drug meant to boost our powers.


00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:17.648
My name is Cassie Holmes.


00:05:18.284 --> 00:05:19.876
Division took my mom from me.


00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:22.917
Right now the future I
see doesn't look so great.


00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:25.981
The good news is the
future is always changing...


00:05:26.326 --> 00:05:30.023
in the largest of ways
by the smallest of things.


00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.761
They've been winning
a lot of battles.


00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:35.633
Now it's our turn
to win the war.


00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:39.868
"TODAY"


00:05:42.642 --> 00:05:44.269
"DIVISION LAB"


00:07:14.333 --> 00:07:15.994
She survived the injection.


00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:20.664
She's our patient zero. Bring
me every sniffer we have.


00:07:20.773 --> 00:07:22.866
But she's on foot.
She can't get far.


00:07:24.877 --> 00:07:27.402
She'll get help from anyone
she can lay her eyes on.


00:07:30.917 --> 00:07:34.444
Do whatever is necessary to get
her and that syringe back! Now!


00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:40.584
"2 DAYS FROM NOW"


00:09:20.593 --> 00:09:25.587
You're already down five thousand I
hear you owe more than that to Chen.


00:09:27.033 --> 00:09:28.057
Chen's a liar...


00:09:28.134 --> 00:09:31.001
Am I a liar too? I was told...


00:09:31.103 --> 00:09:32.934
you owe fifteen


00:09:33.039 --> 00:09:35.234
So you want to bet or not?


00:09:35.942 --> 00:09:37.876
Ok. But if you lose again...


00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:39.443
I'll have you beaten.


00:10:18.517 --> 00:10:21.645
You owe us six thousand, Nick!


00:10:58.090 --> 00:10:59.387
What do you say, Nick?


00:11:01.127 --> 00:11:01.923
Who are you?


00:11:02.028 --> 00:11:03.962
- We're with Division.
- Like you didn't know.


00:11:05.131 --> 00:11:06.297
- Go to hell.
- Easy, son.


00:11:06.332 --> 00:11:08.300
If we wanted you, you'd
be in the back of a van.


00:11:08.367 --> 00:11:10.665
You gonna let us in or are
we gonna have to be rude?


00:11:14.373 --> 00:11:16.568
Smart move living in
a shithole like this.


00:11:17.243 --> 00:11:20.007
One on top of the other.
Took you far off the radar.


00:11:20.079 --> 00:11:21.307
Not far enough.


00:11:24.884 --> 00:11:26.476
Would you believe this
is how we found you?


00:11:26.552 --> 00:11:29.521
From your old toothbrush from
that encounter ten years ago.


00:11:29.655 --> 00:11:30.952
Barely a scent left.


00:11:35.761 --> 00:11:37.160
Thought you were in Tokyo.


00:11:39.932 --> 00:11:41.160
Then Malaysia.


00:11:50.376 --> 00:11:53.607
Finally we got a few
readings on some buildings.


00:12:02.722 --> 00:12:06.852
There's a lot of runaway psychics in
Hong Kong trying to disappear. Nick.


00:12:07.359 --> 00:12:10.328
People with no
country, no loyalty...


00:12:10.429 --> 00:12:13.296
No desire to get involved
in political bullshit.


00:12:29.548 --> 00:12:31.812
Nobody but you in this
apartment for a long time, Nick.


00:12:31.917 --> 00:12:33.646
Why? You looking for
someone besides me?


00:12:34.186 --> 00:12:37.155
A girl. She has
something belonging to us.


00:12:37.957 --> 00:12:39.481
Better than a
hunch you know her.


00:12:42.328 --> 00:12:43.886
Obviously I don't.


00:12:48.667 --> 00:12:50.567
In case we need to
get hold of you again.


00:12:50.669 --> 00:12:53.331
I've got some old toilet
paper you boys might like more.


00:12:53.906 --> 00:12:55.533
Don't bother running.


00:12:56.909 --> 00:12:58.399
We know where you are now.


00:13:07.553 --> 00:13:09.020
Shit.


00:13:34.513 --> 00:13:35.878
- Yeah?
- Hey, Nick.


00:13:36.215 --> 00:13:37.944
- Who is this?
- Open up, Nick.


00:13:38.584 --> 00:13:40.279
And put your gun down.


00:13:53.833 --> 00:13:56.825
Put that thing away.
Got you something.


00:13:58.604 --> 00:14:01.072
Where's the
chicken...? There it is.


00:14:03.709 --> 00:14:06.303
Hey, whoa! Excuse me?


00:14:07.313 --> 00:14:08.678
Is this how you
treat your guests?


00:14:08.747 --> 00:14:12.740
This is how I treat random strangers
who barge into my apartment.


00:14:12.885 --> 00:14:15.046
Like the Division sniffers
who were just here?


00:14:16.055 --> 00:14:17.044
Who are you?


00:14:18.023 --> 00:14:19.490
I'm Cassie.


00:14:20.726 --> 00:14:22.057
I'm here to help you.


00:14:24.330 --> 00:14:25.695
Listen, Cassie...


00:14:25.764 --> 00:14:28.699
I'm sure your mom and dad are nervous
about you right now, so why don't you...


00:14:29.435 --> 00:14:31.369
- You don't understand.
- You've got that right.


00:14:32.304 --> 00:14:34.670
This is about us finding
six million dollars.


00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:38.804
That's us.


00:14:40.646 --> 00:14:42.011
And that's our money.


00:14:44.483 --> 00:14:46.075
And that's my toothbrush.


00:14:46.652 --> 00:14:47.846
You're a watcher.


00:14:49.655 --> 00:14:51.885
So is there a place we can get
something to eat besides chicken?


00:14:55.327 --> 00:14:56.487
I'm buying.


00:15:10.709 --> 00:15:12.199
Lose a bet with
your hairdresser?


00:15:12.945 --> 00:15:14.173
I like color.


00:15:57.423 --> 00:16:00.654
First things first. I know
you're a second-generation mover.


00:16:00.726 --> 00:16:02.284
Is that what the kids
are calling it these days?


00:16:02.361 --> 00:16:03.692
I'll let you know
when I see one.


00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:05.297
You don't really
use your powers,


00:16:05.364 --> 00:16:07.127
which means you haven't practiced
and you kind of suck at it.


00:16:07.199 --> 00:16:08.689
- How am I doing so far?
- Go on.


00:16:08.767 --> 00:16:09.893
I'm a watcher.


00:16:10.803 --> 00:16:12.361
Second generation, like you.


00:16:12.471 --> 00:16:14.336
- Wow. That's.
- Complicated.


00:16:14.673 --> 00:16:16.664
Because the future can change
just by talking about it.


00:16:16.775 --> 00:16:18.402
So I see glimpses
and I draw in my book.


00:16:18.510 --> 00:16:20.000
But I'm not really good at it.


00:16:20.079 --> 00:16:21.774
I'm kind of a
crappy artist, but...


00:16:22.314 --> 00:16:23.838
I'm sure you
already knew that.


00:16:25.985 --> 00:16:27.748
But I got the sniffs in
your apartment, right?


00:16:28.053 --> 00:16:29.611
That's why I brought
you a new toothbrush.


00:16:31.323 --> 00:16:32.483
Anything with shrimp.


00:16:33.525 --> 00:16:34.719
You speak Chinese?


00:16:34.994 --> 00:16:37.690
Cantonese. I'm surprised
you didn't know that,


00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:39.022
being a watcher.


00:16:39.164 --> 00:16:40.893
I get things wrong sometimes.


00:16:41.166 --> 00:16:42.190
I know the feeling.


00:16:45.170 --> 00:16:47.070
Are you worried about the
thugs you owe money to?


00:16:48.073 --> 00:16:49.734
Don't. Thank you.


00:16:49.875 --> 00:16:51.672
We'll be able to take care
of it in a couple days.


00:16:53.278 --> 00:16:55.269
With your six million dollars.


00:16:56.348 --> 00:16:58.282
- Where's the money?
- It's on its way here.


00:16:59.318 --> 00:17:00.410
With a girl.


00:17:01.754 --> 00:17:02.743
Don't tell me.


00:17:02.888 --> 00:17:04.879
Same girl Division
sniffs are looking for.


00:17:08.494 --> 00:17:09.927
It's Cassie, right?


00:17:10.763 --> 00:17:12.128
Enjoy your food.


00:17:13.032 --> 00:17:14.431
- That's it?
- That's it.


00:17:14.566 --> 00:17:17.160
Sorry. Some 12-year old that
knew I needed a new toothbrush...


00:17:17.269 --> 00:17:18.998
isn't enough to get me
involved with Division.


00:17:19.104 --> 00:17:20.401
Even if it's not a con.


00:17:22.307 --> 00:17:25.674
I'm 13. And I've been
told I look at least 14.


00:17:25.811 --> 00:17:27.802
- Right.
- And this is not a con.


00:17:27.913 --> 00:17:30.381
This is a way for everyone
to get something they want.


00:17:30.482 --> 00:17:32.040
I've actually used
that line before.


00:17:32.317 --> 00:17:34.808
Fine. Don't believe me.


00:17:36.155 --> 00:17:38.089
- But you will help me.
- Really?


00:17:38.190 --> 00:17:39.782
Because I'm getting a message.


00:17:39.925 --> 00:17:42.587
It's telling me
"find somebody else".


00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:46.525
If we don't find the
case and that girl,


00:17:46.632 --> 00:17:48.429
really bad things
happen, Nick.


00:17:50.536 --> 00:17:52.834
What? What's wrong?


00:17:57.376 --> 00:18:00.641
Shit. They're
here in the market.


00:18:00.712 --> 00:18:01.838
Who?


00:18:02.681 --> 00:18:04.876
- Who?
- They're in the market! Come on!


00:18:04.950 --> 00:18:06.281
- Division?
- Bleeders!


00:18:06.385 --> 00:18:07.511
We've got to get out of here!


00:18:22.067 --> 00:18:23.329
- How does this end?
- I have no idea.


00:18:23.435 --> 00:18:24.766
Where is the girl?


00:18:25.437 --> 00:18:27.462
My daughter has already
seen you with her.


00:18:27.573 --> 00:18:28.972
Told you.


00:18:30.209 --> 00:18:32.837
I've told three people already
today, I don't know this girl.


00:18:34.713 --> 00:18:37.739
Stupid child. I
already saw how you die.


00:18:37.850 --> 00:18:40.478
Then you know it's not
here and it's not today.


00:18:47.759 --> 00:18:48.851
Damn.


00:18:51.029 --> 00:18:52.496
Go, go!


00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:06.607
Go, go!


00:19:12.351 --> 00:19:13.875
Go, go!


00:19:20.325 --> 00:19:21.883
Nick!


00:19:29.268 --> 00:19:30.860
The big tanks... Go!


00:19:31.603 --> 00:19:33.161
- Quick!
- This way!


00:19:58.430 --> 00:19:59.761
Stop...!


00:20:00.866 --> 00:20:03.300
- Stop...!
- Run, Cassie!


00:20:04.636 --> 00:20:05.830
Stop...!


00:20:21.153 --> 00:20:22.347
Not like this...


00:20:22.721 --> 00:20:24.689
...If we kill him
we lose the girl


00:23:30.275 --> 00:23:32.004
I already know you're here.


00:23:40.519 --> 00:23:42.282
You must be Cassie Holmes.


00:23:43.522 --> 00:23:45.490
- Who sent you?
- Your mother.


00:23:48.126 --> 00:23:50.094
A week before she was
captured by Division,


00:23:50.328 --> 00:23:52.558
she told me to be at
that fish market today.


00:23:54.332 --> 00:23:55.765
Stay away from him.


00:23:56.334 --> 00:23:57.699
If that's what you want.


00:23:57.769 --> 00:24:00.602
Just be sure to add his
picture to the Wall of the Dead.


00:24:02.073 --> 00:24:03.131
You're a stitch.


00:24:03.241 --> 00:24:05.266
That should be
obvious to a watcher.


00:24:06.077 --> 00:24:08.602
If you had even a modicum
of your mother's talent...


00:24:08.713 --> 00:24:10.010
I've been dealing with a lot.


00:24:10.081 --> 00:24:12.948
Years ago your
mother did me a favor.


00:24:13.051 --> 00:24:15.144
Now it would seem I
need to pay off my debt.


00:24:35.307 --> 00:24:38.435
I hear they've got your mother
buried deep inside Division.


00:24:41.246 --> 00:24:44.875
Have her so drugged up she
can't even hold a spoon.


00:24:46.117 --> 00:24:49.109
I bet they suck the
future right out of her.


00:25:24.456 --> 00:25:26.185
You help her and
you help us all.


00:25:27.592 --> 00:25:28.718
A flower


00:25:46.545 --> 00:25:47.876
Is he okay?


00:26:23.715 --> 00:26:26.013
- You okay?
- Yeah.


00:26:30.522 --> 00:26:31.682
Wow.


00:26:32.290 --> 00:26:34.121
That woman's got
magic fingers.


00:26:43.835 --> 00:26:45.132
For you.


00:26:45.870 --> 00:26:47.201
What is that?


00:26:48.640 --> 00:26:49.629
It's a lotus.


00:27:10.729 --> 00:27:12.492
I heard what she said
about your mother.


00:27:14.232 --> 00:27:15.597
You did?


00:27:19.604 --> 00:27:21.128
Division's got her.


00:27:22.040 --> 00:27:25.203
They locked her up because she's the...
greatest watcher they've ever seen.


00:27:26.277 --> 00:27:27.801
They're afraid of her.


00:27:28.146 --> 00:27:30.011
And they're afraid
they can't control her.


00:27:31.683 --> 00:27:33.708
They killed my father
for the same reason.


00:27:36.554 --> 00:27:38.044
But I guess you
already knew that.


00:27:39.524 --> 00:27:42.288
I see the future,
not the past.


00:27:44.095 --> 00:27:47.360
And right now our
future isn't that great.


00:27:49.467 --> 00:27:50.729
That's new?


00:27:51.269 --> 00:27:53.066
Now the sniffs
from your apartment


00:27:53.204 --> 00:27:54.865
are going to get the
girl and the case.


00:27:56.474 --> 00:27:57.839
It's changed.


00:27:58.643 --> 00:28:00.770
I don't know why...


00:28:01.279 --> 00:28:03.770
something I did,
a mistake I made...


00:28:05.083 --> 00:28:08.246
Doesn't matter, it just has.


00:28:11.356 --> 00:28:13.688
My mother told me that case...


00:28:13.825 --> 00:28:17.124
is the key to bringing down
Division and freeing her.


00:28:19.931 --> 00:28:22.229
There's no money in
that case, is there?


00:28:26.438 --> 00:28:28.531
Unless I'm missing something,


00:28:29.641 --> 00:28:31.074
they don't have the case yet.


00:28:32.644 --> 00:28:34.305
It's still out there.


00:28:37.916 --> 00:28:39.508
If your mother's such
a great fortune-teller,


00:28:39.651 --> 00:28:41.084
how did she get caught?


00:28:41.586 --> 00:28:43.713
I'm just going to have
to ask her that myself.


00:28:45.023 --> 00:28:46.923
I haven't even gotten
to the bad part yet.


00:28:50.829 --> 00:28:52.023
What is that?


00:28:53.031 --> 00:28:54.396
We die.


00:28:56.167 --> 00:28:57.725
Great.


00:29:23.328 --> 00:29:24.795
Hello, Kira.


00:29:29.734 --> 00:29:31.031
You have a plane to catch.


00:29:31.369 --> 00:29:33.166
Come on. You want
to come with us.


00:29:47.318 --> 00:29:49.843
Christ. Get a load of that.


00:29:49.954 --> 00:29:54.482
She must use that ten times
a day. That's a keeper.


00:29:54.926 --> 00:29:57.451
You're not gonna have a lot of lipstick
opportunities where you're going.


00:29:57.529 --> 00:29:58.791
You know what I mean?


00:30:02.534 --> 00:30:03.762
She's doing it again.


00:30:03.835 --> 00:30:06.429
- Get the hell out of my head!
- No! No!


00:30:07.372 --> 00:30:09.670
- What does she want?
- She's got to go to the bathroom.


00:30:10.008 --> 00:30:11.566
To throw up or something.


00:30:11.676 --> 00:30:13.871
Carver will kill us if
anything happens to her.


00:30:28.226 --> 00:30:29.887
- Bathroom?
- This way.


00:30:31.996 --> 00:30:33.088
Come on.


00:30:37.135 --> 00:30:39.262
Coffee, black, with sugar.


00:30:53.484 --> 00:30:55.315
Alright. In you go.


00:31:09.200 --> 00:31:10.997
You're a good man, Agent Mack.


00:31:12.604 --> 00:31:14.629
I bet you come
from a good family.


00:31:16.574 --> 00:31:18.804
It must have been hard
for you when he died.


00:31:19.677 --> 00:31:20.837
Who died?


00:31:21.913 --> 00:31:23.244
Your brother.


00:31:23.815 --> 00:31:26.215
- I don't have a brother, sweetheart.
- No, you do.


00:31:27.051 --> 00:31:28.916
I've got something that
will make you feel better.


00:31:29.721 --> 00:31:32.053
And you loved him very much.


00:31:35.693 --> 00:31:37.490
But he was murdered.


00:31:37.629 --> 00:31:40.029
And you know who
did it, don't you?


00:31:51.910 --> 00:31:53.241
But he was murdered...


00:31:53.912 --> 00:31:56.176
And you know who
did it, don't you?


00:32:00.084 --> 00:32:03.611
You know who did it, don't
you? But he was murdered...


00:32:18.136 --> 00:32:21.970
You know who did it
he was murdered...


00:34:25.430 --> 00:34:26.897
Lame.


00:34:27.832 --> 00:34:30.130
We've got to work on your skills
if we're going to change anything.


00:34:30.201 --> 00:34:31.691
Don't bite your nails.


00:34:34.872 --> 00:34:36.863
The lollipop chick
freaks me out.


00:34:38.709 --> 00:34:40.768
- She's a watcher.
- Like you.


00:34:41.679 --> 00:34:42.805
Yeah.


00:34:43.848 --> 00:34:46.442
I know this place. This is...


00:34:47.485 --> 00:34:51.080
I know this place. Club B,
boss. Science Museum Road.


00:34:51.823 --> 00:34:53.085
Thank you.


00:34:54.759 --> 00:34:56.351
Why is that olive
out of the glass?


00:34:57.528 --> 00:35:00.691
- That's not an olive. It's a bead.
- It's a bead?


00:35:01.332 --> 00:35:04.563
Yeah, it's a bead. A
shimmery kind of thing...


00:35:04.669 --> 00:35:07.137
Well, it looks like a pimento. If
I was going to draw a bead, I'd...


00:35:07.238 --> 00:35:09.172
It's a bead with a shimmer.


00:35:09.874 --> 00:35:11.398
What does the bead
have to do with it?


00:35:11.509 --> 00:35:14.069
I don't know what the shiny,
shimmery bead has to do with it.


00:35:14.612 --> 00:35:15.772
Great.


00:35:16.647 --> 00:35:17.978
Let's keep it simple.


00:35:18.316 --> 00:35:20.307
We'll start with the bead
and see where it takes us.


00:35:20.384 --> 00:35:23.820
Sounds like a plan, but... what
about the part where we die?


00:35:39.036 --> 00:35:40.663
I remember growing
up together.


00:35:41.072 --> 00:35:42.869
Where we went to school.


00:35:43.808 --> 00:35:45.105
How he died.


00:35:46.878 --> 00:35:48.869
So except for this
brother you never had...


00:35:49.847 --> 00:35:52.338
is there anything else she
might have put in your head?


00:35:52.783 --> 00:35:54.910
I'm only asking because I don't
want to be shot in the face...


00:35:55.052 --> 00:35:57.543
for screwing some made up
sister you don't really have.


00:35:58.923 --> 00:36:00.288
I don't have a sister?


00:36:07.331 --> 00:36:10.095
Agent Mack, you are
relieved of duty.


00:36:10.201 --> 00:36:12.066
Get on a plane, eat some
peanuts, and go home.


00:36:12.203 --> 00:36:13.534
She won't push me again, sir.


00:36:13.604 --> 00:36:15.003
She just caught me off-guard.


00:36:15.072 --> 00:36:17.632
The only thoughts in
my head are my own.


00:36:18.943 --> 00:36:20.911
You're willing to
risk your life on that?


00:36:21.913 --> 00:36:22.971
Yes, sir.


00:36:23.080 --> 00:36:26.208
Then put the gun in your
mouth and pull the trigger.


00:36:30.121 --> 00:36:31.452
Don't worry.


00:36:31.789 --> 00:36:34.553
You already checked
it. It's not loaded.


00:36:42.633 --> 00:36:45.625
Spread these beads to
any sniff, any watcher,


00:36:45.703 --> 00:36:48.453
any goddamn expatriate
reader in Hong Kong


00:36:48.488 --> 00:36:51.204
who knows up from down
until we find Kira.


00:36:52.410 --> 00:36:54.275
What about the Chinese
government and their guys?


00:36:54.745 --> 00:36:57.771
The story is out, bleeders all over
the country will be looking for her.


00:36:58.216 --> 00:36:59.649
We can't let
them get the drug.


00:37:00.051 --> 00:37:01.882
Then we put a
price on her head.


00:37:09.493 --> 00:37:10.790
Yeah, this is it.


00:37:11.429 --> 00:37:14.296
Hey, can you...
I don't have any...


00:37:14.365 --> 00:37:16.424
Yeah! Sure. I got it.


00:37:18.336 --> 00:37:20.861
There you go. You
can keep it. Thanks.


00:37:24.075 --> 00:37:25.042
How much do you have?


00:37:25.109 --> 00:37:26.474
Don't give him all of that.


00:37:26.544 --> 00:37:28.478
- It's not gonna be enough.
- It's enough.


00:37:28.546 --> 00:37:29.911
- Just give me the...
- It's enough. / Excuse me, sir?


00:37:30.047 --> 00:37:31.241
Hey. We need five minutes.


00:37:31.315 --> 00:37:32.407
- Five minutes
- Yeah!


00:37:34.085 --> 00:37:37.248
Listen, this is a
place for grown-ups,


00:37:37.321 --> 00:37:39.186
- so behave yourself.
- Shut up.


00:37:39.924 --> 00:37:41.255
That sounds about right.


00:37:47.598 --> 00:37:50.567
- Choose another.
- Yeah! Show me...


00:37:50.668 --> 00:37:51.828
- Concentrate.
- Yes.


00:37:52.069 --> 00:37:55.971
- Queen of hearts.
- Okay. Watch. It's already here.


00:37:59.510 --> 00:38:03.412
Show me... Ace of spades.


00:38:08.119 --> 00:38:09.450
Think I know why we're here.


00:38:12.223 --> 00:38:13.690
You've got good hands.


00:38:13.758 --> 00:38:15.919
- Nick! You alright?
- Yeah.


00:38:16.027 --> 00:38:18.257
What's going on? Sit down.


00:38:19.764 --> 00:38:21.391
- Vodka martini?
- Thank you.


00:38:21.532 --> 00:38:22.692
I'll have one of those.


00:38:23.768 --> 00:38:24.894
She'll have a Coke.


00:38:25.002 --> 00:38:27.163
My mom drinks when she wants
to get really clear images.


00:38:27.305 --> 00:38:28.465
She's famous for it.


00:38:29.106 --> 00:38:30.630
Maybe something
without caffeine.


00:38:31.042 --> 00:38:32.475
I've got it. Whoa.


00:38:33.344 --> 00:38:34.709
There's five.


00:38:36.213 --> 00:38:37.407
Keep the change.


00:38:37.515 --> 00:38:38.482
Thank you.


00:38:41.919 --> 00:38:43.113
I know who you are.


00:38:45.323 --> 00:38:46.688
When I was in Division,


00:38:46.791 --> 00:38:49.783
her mother was at the top of
every watch list there was.


00:38:50.928 --> 00:38:52.088
You worked for Division?


00:38:55.833 --> 00:38:57.528
You want to know
about Division?


00:38:59.236 --> 00:39:02.330
Ten years. No thank
you, no pension.


00:39:02.440 --> 00:39:05.273
I was put out on the street
with a threat to not shift again.


00:39:07.044 --> 00:39:08.978
Only the sniffs caught
up with me in Chicago.


00:39:09.080 --> 00:39:12.015
I was just trying to buy
something nice for my wife.


00:39:13.284 --> 00:39:16.014
Next day I get a
call, she's dead.


00:39:16.954 --> 00:39:18.512
Car accident.


00:39:19.757 --> 00:39:22.692
But my wife doesn't drive.


00:39:25.730 --> 00:39:28.893
But I don't have to remind
you how that feels, right?


00:39:35.873 --> 00:39:38.171
- We need this.
- An olive?


00:39:39.310 --> 00:39:40.709
It's a bead.


00:39:41.912 --> 00:39:44.881
It's supposed to lead us to someone
we need to find before Division does.


00:39:46.484 --> 00:39:48.418
Excuse me! May I?


00:39:50.921 --> 00:39:52.115
Thank you.


00:39:52.790 --> 00:39:54.052
You're welcome.


00:39:58.496 --> 00:39:59.520
Got it right?


00:40:00.564 --> 00:40:02.964
It's a little more
round and shinier.


00:40:04.268 --> 00:40:05.667
That's it.


00:40:05.970 --> 00:40:07.437
That's just how I saw it.


00:40:10.040 --> 00:40:11.598
It won't last long.


00:40:11.709 --> 00:40:15.440
I'd take it Emily Hu.
She's ex-pat sniff.


00:40:15.746 --> 00:40:18.237
Only works by referral.
Here's her address.


00:40:19.917 --> 00:40:21.282
Thank you, Hook.


00:40:22.920 --> 00:40:24.114
Bye bye.


00:40:25.389 --> 00:40:26.788
Good luck.


00:40:36.000 --> 00:40:37.433
Here it is...


00:40:42.807 --> 00:40:44.775
Is she with someone else?


00:40:57.087 --> 00:40:58.554
Yes


00:40:59.690 --> 00:41:03.524
I see a man... and a boat


00:41:03.727 --> 00:41:05.319
Is she happy?


00:41:05.963 --> 00:41:07.624
Will she come back?


00:41:07.731 --> 00:41:10.427
It's a very big boat.


00:41:17.908 --> 00:41:18.875
May I help you?


00:41:19.009 --> 00:41:20.636
Hook Waters sent us.


00:41:21.879 --> 00:41:24.973
A bead that looks like this one
is supposed to lead us to a girl.


00:41:32.356 --> 00:41:33.721
You with Division?


00:41:34.925 --> 00:41:36.483
Are you looking at us?


00:41:37.761 --> 00:41:39.820
The truth is, the girl
who dropped that bead...


00:41:39.930 --> 00:41:42.490
is supposed to have a suitcase
that will bring down Division.


00:41:42.566 --> 00:41:45.865
Cassie here thinks that if
we don't find it, we die.


00:41:46.036 --> 00:41:47.526
And you believe her?


00:41:49.173 --> 00:41:50.800
She's pretty convincing.


00:41:50.908 --> 00:41:53.274
Well, consider me unconvinced.


00:42:01.085 --> 00:42:03.076
Looks like we've
just got to wait.


00:42:03.254 --> 00:42:04.278
For what?


00:42:04.355 --> 00:42:06.118
You have about one
minute to help us.


00:42:08.125 --> 00:42:09.319
And what's that?


00:42:09.493 --> 00:42:12.053
That's your... poster.


00:42:13.330 --> 00:42:15.491
- That's the bead.
- That's the clock.


00:42:16.267 --> 00:42:18.394
- It's... right now...
- You've got about a minute.


00:42:21.872 --> 00:42:23.669
You guys can't be serious.


00:42:23.774 --> 00:42:25.071
Don't look at me.


00:42:25.309 --> 00:42:27.470
This girl's been going at
it with that plan all day.


00:42:27.678 --> 00:42:30.374
Everything that ends up on this
pad seems to be coming true.


00:42:30.714 --> 00:42:32.875
I just see it like I'm
looking at a photograph.


00:42:37.187 --> 00:42:39.553
Look... we want Division
out of Hong Kong...


00:42:39.690 --> 00:42:41.157
just as much as you do.


00:42:41.525 --> 00:42:44.551
It's going to be a whole lot
easier if you help us find the girl.


00:42:45.763 --> 00:42:47.993
You remind me of someone...


00:42:48.065 --> 00:42:49.930
...I used to know


00:42:54.705 --> 00:42:56.036
Fine.


00:42:59.710 --> 00:43:02.474
They've been spreading
these all over the city.


00:43:14.558 --> 00:43:19.086
You'll find who you're
looking for on Kwun Tong Pier.


00:43:50.794 --> 00:43:52.091
Excuse me!


00:43:53.597 --> 00:43:56.623
Excuse me. Speak any English?


00:43:56.734 --> 00:43:57.894
- No.
- No.


00:43:58.002 --> 00:44:02.234
It doesn't really matter.
I just need a ride.


00:44:04.308 --> 00:44:05.775
We're old friends, right?


00:44:12.750 --> 00:44:15.548
I know. I should have called.


00:44:32.636 --> 00:44:33.864
Whoa, whoa!


00:44:34.905 --> 00:44:37.271
- Kira?
- Dammit!


00:44:37.408 --> 00:44:39.376
- What the hell are you doing here?
- There goes my ride!


00:44:39.943 --> 00:44:42.104
- Don't.
- Don't. Don't what?


00:44:42.312 --> 00:44:43.836
You're the girl
everyone's looking for?


00:44:43.914 --> 00:44:45.279
- I should kill you, Nick.
- Hey!


00:44:45.449 --> 00:44:46.746
You know this psycho?


00:44:46.884 --> 00:44:48.545
- What happened to you?
- Now you want to know?


00:44:49.086 --> 00:44:50.917
What does that mean?
I thought you left.


00:44:51.055 --> 00:44:52.044
You stopped
returning my calls.


00:44:52.156 --> 00:44:53.885
Division caught me
and locked me up.


00:44:53.991 --> 00:44:55.891
- What?
- And you never came.


00:44:55.959 --> 00:44:58.086
I looked for you. I did!


00:45:00.064 --> 00:45:01.326
You didn't find me.


00:45:02.232 --> 00:45:05.030
It's done! You had
a thing. Get over it.


00:45:05.335 --> 00:45:07.929
I really suggest we
discuss this somewhere else.


00:45:09.440 --> 00:45:10.805
Let's go, Nick.


00:45:24.722 --> 00:45:26.986
Kira. Division's
looking for you.


00:45:27.558 --> 00:45:29.389
They're looking for the case.


00:45:29.927 --> 00:45:31.155
And so are you.


00:45:31.595 --> 00:45:33.085
What's in that case?


00:45:33.664 --> 00:45:34.926
I don't know.


00:45:35.332 --> 00:45:36.822
All I know is that
I woke up on a boat


00:45:36.934 --> 00:45:39.027
next to a note I'd written
saying to look for you


00:45:39.103 --> 00:45:40.866
and you'd help
me find the case.


00:45:43.107 --> 00:45:45.667
I don't remember anything
about the last couple of days...


00:45:46.310 --> 00:45:48.175
no matter how hard I try.


00:45:48.946 --> 00:45:50.504
You must have had
yourself wiped.


00:45:51.515 --> 00:45:54.075
Erased memories make it harder
for Division to track you.


00:45:56.720 --> 00:45:58.244
Not the ones of you.


00:46:01.725 --> 00:46:03.249
Can I talk to you for a sec?


00:46:04.094 --> 00:46:05.288
Can it wait?


00:46:05.629 --> 00:46:06.721
I'm kind of in the
middle of something.


00:46:06.830 --> 00:46:08.024
No.


00:46:12.770 --> 00:46:14.465
You, me, and my mom.


00:46:15.472 --> 00:46:17.667
I've never seen my
mom's death before.


00:46:18.842 --> 00:46:20.070
It's her, Nick.


00:46:20.711 --> 00:46:23.475
She's changing the future,
and she's making it worse.


00:46:23.614 --> 00:46:25.172
- We've got to dump her.
- Dump her?


00:46:25.516 --> 00:46:26.813
Cassie, we...


00:46:28.118 --> 00:46:29.483
Cassie! We just found her.


00:46:29.586 --> 00:46:31.110
And she doesn't have the case.


00:46:31.188 --> 00:46:32.155
Which is what
we're looking for,


00:46:32.289 --> 00:46:33.722
- if you remember.
- Yeah! I know.


00:46:34.958 --> 00:46:36.858
We find her, we find the case.


00:46:36.927 --> 00:46:39.157
- The three of us.
- Yeah, and then Division finds her.


00:46:39.329 --> 00:46:41.024
Oh yeah, the three of us.


00:46:44.268 --> 00:46:46.463
We'll get a shadow so
they can't trace her.


00:46:46.570 --> 00:46:48.231
- Satisfied?
- No.


00:46:50.307 --> 00:46:51.638
Cassie, you've
got to trust me.


00:46:51.708 --> 00:46:53.642
I'm not the one with
the trust issues here.


00:46:53.710 --> 00:46:54.870
You better do something quick


00:46:54.945 --> 00:46:57.175
because I'm getting sick
of drawing dead bodies.


00:47:26.910 --> 00:47:28.172
That's him.


00:47:29.546 --> 00:47:30.979
- Hey, Pinky.
- Hey, Nick.


00:47:31.081 --> 00:47:33.641
- Hey.
- Alright, who's feeling the heat?


00:47:35.986 --> 00:47:37.283
Alright.


00:47:38.188 --> 00:47:39.485
Here's how this works:


00:47:39.556 --> 00:47:41.990
I get ten grand a day for
shadowing Miss Trouble.


00:47:42.092 --> 00:47:43.889
As long as she stays
within twenty feet of me,


00:47:43.961 --> 00:47:45.451
no sniff is gonna find her.


00:47:45.529 --> 00:47:46.553
I don't care if they're
standing right on top


00:47:46.630 --> 00:47:48.359
of us with a piece
of her fingernail.


00:47:48.932 --> 00:47:51.025
- Happy?
- Overcome.


00:47:51.335 --> 00:47:53.428
Come on. Let's find
a place to think.


00:47:56.473 --> 00:48:00.000
So Pinky, your wife
give you that name?


00:48:00.644 --> 00:48:02.635
No, the Division
did, sweetheart.


00:48:03.480 --> 00:48:04.777
Back in the day.


00:48:13.724 --> 00:48:16.852
I'm sorry. I can't remember
anything about the case.


00:48:17.361 --> 00:48:18.953
Shocking.


00:48:22.332 --> 00:48:24.493
Can I clean up
without getting killed?


00:48:24.568 --> 00:48:26.593
Don't forget to wash
behind your ears.


00:48:30.874 --> 00:48:32.432
Nice girlfriend
you've got there.


00:48:32.509 --> 00:48:35.273
Yeah. She used to be.


00:48:35.345 --> 00:48:38.280
I met her running cons
on Coney Island tourists.


00:48:39.316 --> 00:48:41.307
We did everything
together. Everything.


00:48:41.385 --> 00:48:42.818
So we're just gonna sit around


00:48:42.920 --> 00:48:44.649
and wait for her to
get her memory back...


00:48:44.721 --> 00:48:47.690
and hope that she'll tell us where
the case is before Carver gets it?


00:48:48.692 --> 00:48:50.091
Or us.


00:48:50.928 --> 00:48:52.327
Great plan.


00:48:52.829 --> 00:48:54.023
Where you going?


00:48:54.231 --> 00:48:56.791
I saw a chicken place
downstairs. Want to come?


00:48:56.934 --> 00:48:59.425
No, I'm good. I want to
stay here, see if I can help.


00:48:59.503 --> 00:49:00.800
Have fun with that.


00:49:20.958 --> 00:49:22.118
Where you going?


00:49:23.160 --> 00:49:24.388
Relax, Romeo.


00:49:24.528 --> 00:49:26.723
I can shade her just
fine out in the hall.


00:49:28.332 --> 00:49:30.527
I don't need to be a watcher
to see where this is going.


00:50:21.318 --> 00:50:23.149
Oh! Sorry about that.


00:50:23.920 --> 00:50:26.480
I thought the
bathroom was on fire.


00:50:26.590 --> 00:50:29.320
I had to get you
to come in somehow.


00:50:30.327 --> 00:50:31.589
Did you push me?


00:50:31.728 --> 00:50:33.025
You didn't like it?


00:50:35.065 --> 00:50:36.589
Push back.


00:51:12.536 --> 00:51:15.334
My father expects me
to find that suitcase.


00:51:15.405 --> 00:51:16.667
So does my mother.


00:51:17.074 --> 00:51:19.474
But you don't see
it clearly, do you?


00:51:19.943 --> 00:51:21.638
Too many things keep changing.


00:51:22.946 --> 00:51:24.971
I already saw how you die.


00:51:25.849 --> 00:51:27.282
Did you see it yet?


00:51:32.355 --> 00:51:33.879
You can change it, you know.


00:51:33.990 --> 00:51:36.481
Plenty of planes leaving
Hong Kong every day.


00:51:36.560 --> 00:51:38.289
Oh, we are going to change it.


00:51:38.795 --> 00:51:40.820
You put a shadow on the girl.


00:51:41.832 --> 00:51:43.959
You know that's
only temporary.


00:51:44.768 --> 00:51:48.465
That girl is the one who brings all
your little fantasies crashing down.


00:51:49.072 --> 00:51:51.404
So tell Nick something
for me, little girl.


00:51:51.842 --> 00:51:55.243
Tell him my family is going to
make his brain pop like a tomato.


00:51:55.545 --> 00:51:58.309
Tell him that's
the future I see.


00:52:13.263 --> 00:52:14.696
Oh, boy.


00:52:16.833 --> 00:52:18.027
Hello?


00:52:19.636 --> 00:52:22.196
There you are. Where
is the chicky-chicky...


00:52:22.305 --> 00:52:24.170
- who gets us all killed?
- Are you drunk?


00:52:24.241 --> 00:52:25.333
Yeah.


00:52:25.976 --> 00:52:28.274
I'm sorry. I didn't know the procedure
for stopping a blitzed ten-year-old.


00:52:28.345 --> 00:52:32.281
I'm thirteen! And I
am powering my use!


00:52:32.349 --> 00:52:34.317
I can't believe this.


00:52:34.352 --> 00:52:35.614
I am working.


00:52:36.586 --> 00:52:39.282
- You screw it all up!
- Alright...


00:52:39.356 --> 00:52:41.449
Give me this. What is this?
We talked about this, Cassie.


00:52:41.525 --> 00:52:42.549
Nobody is going anywhere.


00:52:42.626 --> 00:52:44.491
- What is this?
- You don't get it, Nick.


00:52:45.829 --> 00:52:48.195
She is the one that
kills us all, basically.


00:52:48.331 --> 00:52:49.298
Then I guess we're
all gonna get killed.


00:52:49.366 --> 00:52:50.833
Yeah. Screwed up.


00:52:50.934 --> 00:52:53.027
By "we", you mean not...


00:52:53.103 --> 00:52:54.195
You, too.


00:52:55.672 --> 00:52:58.334
Pop Girl's a better
watcher than I am.


00:52:58.475 --> 00:53:00.773
Whoa! No one said
anything about a watcher.


00:53:00.844 --> 00:53:02.869
I can only work long-term
against the sniffs.


00:53:02.946 --> 00:53:05.244
- Good.
- No! True story.


00:53:05.315 --> 00:53:07.647
You've got a watcher after
you. It's just a matter of time.


00:53:08.919 --> 00:53:11.353
Then we'll split up.


00:53:11.488 --> 00:53:13.854
We'll give her two things
to track instead of one.


00:53:13.924 --> 00:53:17.360
- Pinky, take Kira somewhere safe
- I'm not going with him.


00:53:17.527 --> 00:53:18.687
No offense.


00:53:18.795 --> 00:53:20.319
None taken, cupcake.


00:53:20.463 --> 00:53:22.021
I know you're
sweet on the champ.


00:53:22.566 --> 00:53:23.794
I'll find you.


00:53:36.880 --> 00:53:38.575
Let's let her sleep for a bit.


00:53:54.123 --> 00:53:55.988
She's a step ahead
of our sister.


00:53:56.058 --> 00:53:57.326
Father will be displeased...


00:53:57.361 --> 00:53:58.691
She saw me coming.


00:54:01.530 --> 00:54:03.088
Maybe she's better than you?


00:54:04.367 --> 00:54:05.891
She still dies!


00:54:13.743 --> 00:54:15.301
She's gone, you know.


00:54:18.114 --> 00:54:19.775
I'm just saying...


00:54:23.286 --> 00:54:25.584
- You okay?
- No...


00:54:27.523 --> 00:54:29.457
Not until we find that case.


00:54:30.226 --> 00:54:31.693
When was the last
time you saw it?


00:54:31.827 --> 00:54:33.124
Not since yesterday.


00:54:33.896 --> 00:54:36.194
Not for lack of
trying, though.


00:54:37.867 --> 00:54:41.359
If we don't find it soon,
they're gonna kill my mom.


00:54:42.338 --> 00:54:43.828
And it's gonna be my fault.


00:55:00.990 --> 00:55:02.355
Look at me.


00:55:02.925 --> 00:55:04.483
Hey! Look at me.


00:55:05.127 --> 00:55:06.685
You really think I'm
gonna let that happen?


00:55:08.464 --> 00:55:10.056
You said the future's
always changing, right?


00:55:10.166 --> 00:55:11.190
It can change
just by knowing it?


00:55:11.267 --> 00:55:14.293
It can change. It
doesn't mean it will.


00:55:17.740 --> 00:55:19.332
- Good enough.
- What are you doing?


00:55:19.909 --> 00:55:20.967
What are you gonna go do?


00:55:21.043 --> 00:55:22.476
I'm gonna try and
make a better one.


00:55:23.746 --> 00:55:25.714
Going after Carver
doesn't change anything.


00:55:25.881 --> 00:55:27.371
It doesn't save me,
it doesn't save you,


00:55:27.450 --> 00:55:28.576
it doesn't save her.


00:55:28.684 --> 00:55:30.447
It's just a matter
of time, Cassie.


00:55:30.553 --> 00:55:32.418
If I don't go to him,
he'll come for us.


00:55:41.764 --> 00:55:42.890
Emily, it's Nick.


00:55:43.933 --> 00:55:46.060
Division sent a pusher
named Carver to Hong Kong.


00:55:46.168 --> 00:55:47.328
I need you to find him.


00:55:49.705 --> 00:55:52.606
Just use that bead they gave you.
I'm sure his hands were all over it.


00:56:21.137 --> 00:56:23.435
- We're not open.
- I'm not hungry.


00:57:21.330 --> 00:57:22.854
Henry Carver.


00:57:26.802 --> 00:57:29.669
Now there's a face I
haven't seen in a long time.


00:57:35.911 --> 00:57:37.378
Sit down.


00:57:37.847 --> 00:57:40.042
The food is actually
pretty good here.


00:57:46.021 --> 00:57:48.546
Give me one good reason
not to kill you right now.


00:57:50.726 --> 00:57:51.920
Good.


00:57:52.361 --> 00:57:54.226
Gonna try and get
inside my head?


00:57:55.097 --> 00:57:56.462
Go ahead.


00:57:56.532 --> 00:57:59.126
See if you can push me
before I pull the trigger.


00:58:00.603 --> 00:58:04.539
Wow! Ten years is a long
time to hold a grudge.


00:58:04.673 --> 00:58:06.334
My father would disagree.


00:58:06.542 --> 00:58:10.603
- You piece of shit.
- Your father I had respect for.


00:58:10.713 --> 00:58:12.908
He took a stand
with great integrity,


00:58:12.982 --> 00:58:15.542
which is more than
anyone can say about you.


00:58:20.723 --> 00:58:23.385
- If this is your attempt at...
- Think I don't know this future?


00:58:24.059 --> 00:58:25.287
Huh?


00:58:25.361 --> 00:58:28.387
I've got twenty of the best
watchers in the world...


00:58:28.497 --> 00:58:31.432
tracking every moment
of this time right now.


00:58:32.935 --> 00:58:34.459
You die, Nick.


00:58:35.771 --> 00:58:37.363
You all die.


00:58:37.907 --> 00:58:39.306
You know who doesn't?


00:58:41.243 --> 00:58:43.108
- Me.
- You sure about that?


00:58:45.748 --> 00:58:47.306
Okay.


00:58:48.350 --> 00:58:50.511
Kira is our patient zero.


00:58:50.953 --> 00:58:53.979
And with her we're going to
create an army the world's


00:58:54.089 --> 00:58:56.725
- never seen before...
- I'm sorry. Am I supposed to care?


00:58:56.760 --> 00:59:00.092
Fine. Fuck patriotism.


00:59:00.496 --> 00:59:03.693
The girl will die unless she
receives the necessary injections.


00:59:05.401 --> 00:59:08.097
And you're not going to
find it anywhere but with me.


00:59:10.406 --> 00:59:12.203
Maybe you care about that.


00:59:16.378 --> 00:59:17.811
Tell me something, Nick.


00:59:18.747 --> 00:59:21.045
Her blood turn black yet?


00:59:22.484 --> 00:59:24.714
No? Insides running out?


00:59:28.824 --> 00:59:31.224
Or is she keeping that
away from you, too?


00:59:37.700 --> 00:59:39.759
I'll take that as a yes.


01:01:51.033 --> 01:01:53.524
You already know the
ending to this story.


01:01:53.669 --> 01:01:55.728
You can only draw
it so many ways.


01:01:58.774 --> 01:02:00.332
We're going to change it.


01:02:03.746 --> 01:02:05.577
You don't believe
that, do you?


01:02:06.148 --> 01:02:07.547
Please...


01:02:09.084 --> 01:02:11.609
don't make me do
anything to myself.


01:02:12.621 --> 01:02:14.782
Hurting you would
change the future.


01:02:15.624 --> 01:02:17.683
And I like how
this future goes.


01:02:18.660 --> 01:02:20.025
So will killing him.


01:02:36.145 --> 01:02:37.407
Victor!


01:02:57.666 --> 01:02:59.531
I think I just
saved your life.


01:03:00.769 --> 01:03:03.499
There's no need to thank me. You
should just start listening to me.


01:03:10.012 --> 01:03:11.309
You look like shit.


01:03:30.766 --> 01:03:32.529
- Where is
she? - 5-A.


01:03:32.668 --> 01:03:34.329
- Is she safe?
- Yeah.


01:03:34.403 --> 01:03:36.496
She's sick,
though. Pretty bad.


01:04:25.053 --> 01:04:26.850
I need to ask you a question.


01:04:29.091 --> 01:04:30.615
What's in the case?


01:04:35.631 --> 01:04:37.895
It's a drug.


01:04:38.467 --> 01:04:42.267
Some sort of psychic steroid
that boosts our abilities...


01:04:42.871 --> 01:04:44.236
but kills us.


01:04:48.977 --> 01:04:50.706
They want me back


01:04:50.812 --> 01:04:53.781
because I'm the only one...
who survived the injection.


01:04:59.321 --> 01:05:01.619
Tell me why I just drew a
picture of me holding her shoe.


01:05:15.771 --> 01:05:16.931
Is she okay?


01:05:18.874 --> 01:05:21.508
What? No. You've
got to be kidding me.


01:05:21.543 --> 01:05:23.408
- She's dying.
- You are not bringing me into this.


01:05:23.946 --> 01:05:25.072
You're already in it.


01:05:25.647 --> 01:05:27.512
We need to know what
this key unlocks.


01:05:28.417 --> 01:05:29.714
Please.


01:05:31.954 --> 01:05:33.888
Cassie, how much
do the Chinese know?


01:05:34.089 --> 01:05:35.784
Whatever we do.
It could be more.


01:05:36.425 --> 01:05:37.892
Their watcher is
better than me.


01:05:38.026 --> 01:05:40.460
We know there's a suitcase
with a Division drug in it.


01:05:40.529 --> 01:05:42.019
Kira hid it somewhere
in Hong Kong.


01:05:42.097 --> 01:05:43.189
Can you draw us
a way out of this?


01:05:43.298 --> 01:05:45.095
We can't change anything
with that bitch tracking us.


01:05:45.233 --> 01:05:46.700
The second we do,
she's gonna see it.


01:05:46.768 --> 01:05:48.737
- What do you mean?
- She sees intentions.


01:05:48.772 --> 01:05:50.295
What we decide to do.


01:05:50.372 --> 01:05:53.102
I decide to cross the street, so
she sees me crossing the street.


01:05:53.608 --> 01:05:55.508
What if nothing
we did made sense?


01:05:56.411 --> 01:05:57.742
Or we just kept
changing our mind,


01:05:57.813 --> 01:05:59.906
we didn't know exactly
what we were gonna do?


01:06:00.349 --> 01:06:01.714
Would that throw her off?


01:06:01.783 --> 01:06:03.978
It might, but we still
have to find the case.


01:06:15.097 --> 01:06:17.588
Whatever this key
unlocks is being shadowed.


01:06:18.066 --> 01:06:19.897
Like I've never seen before.


01:06:21.269 --> 01:06:22.634
It's this way.


01:06:27.342 --> 01:06:29.003
That really narrows it down.


01:06:33.348 --> 01:06:35.543
If it's shadowed, I
won't be able to draw.


01:06:46.695 --> 01:06:48.390
There's a building missing.


01:06:54.903 --> 01:06:55.892
I thought shadows
weren't supposed


01:06:55.971 --> 01:06:57.871
to be effective against
watchers like Cassie.


01:06:57.939 --> 01:06:59.270
They're not.


01:06:59.941 --> 01:07:02.967
We're not supposed to be able
to shade entire buildings either.


01:07:27.736 --> 01:07:29.499
You wanted to see me?


01:07:32.941 --> 01:07:34.533
I'm going to need your help.


01:07:38.980 --> 01:07:41.107
Watchers from everywhere
are tracking us.


01:07:41.183 --> 01:07:42.741
Carver... the Chinese...


01:07:42.818 --> 01:07:44.547
Anything we think we're
gonna do, they know about it.


01:07:44.653 --> 01:07:47.053
That's why we all keep
dying in Cassie's book.


01:07:47.622 --> 01:07:50.250
- Pardon?
- You die outside an elevator.


01:07:51.226 --> 01:07:52.659
Oh.


01:07:54.096 --> 01:07:56.428
How are we gonna make
the future unpredictable?


01:07:56.531 --> 01:07:58.499
By not knowing
what we're gonna do


01:07:59.267 --> 01:08:00.700
until right before we do it.


01:08:00.769 --> 01:08:03.704
- Like a plan without planning.
- Yes. Right.


01:08:04.005 --> 01:08:05.063
Okay!


01:08:05.907 --> 01:08:09.172
I'll write letters to each of you
giving you specific instruction.


01:08:09.845 --> 01:08:11.608
You don't open them
until I tell you.


01:08:14.282 --> 01:08:16.842
Then the last letter,
I write to myself...


01:08:18.353 --> 01:08:20.287
and wipe the memory of
ever having written them.


01:08:20.422 --> 01:08:22.788
That's why I need you to
find the guy that wiped Kira.


01:08:23.692 --> 01:08:26.183
- Sure thing.
- That sounds like a great plan.


01:08:27.696 --> 01:08:30.221
- Do you have a better one?
- We're flying blind.


01:08:30.532 --> 01:08:31.658
Yeah.


01:08:33.969 --> 01:08:35.266
Cassie...


01:08:35.470 --> 01:08:37.335
I need one more
drawing out of you.


01:08:37.672 --> 01:08:40.664
I need to know the exact
size and shape of that case.


01:08:40.809 --> 01:08:42.276
And that syringe.


01:09:50.612 --> 01:09:53.206
Our watchers say
it is already here.


01:09:53.782 --> 01:09:54.976
Father...


01:09:55.083 --> 01:09:57.643
I know what Division
is looking for...


01:09:57.752 --> 01:09:59.014
It's a syringe.


01:10:01.089 --> 01:10:04.581
with this drug we'll be
more powerful than Division.


01:10:23.044 --> 01:10:27.105
The girl will die unless she
receives the necessary injections.


01:10:27.649 --> 01:10:30.948
You're not going to find the
stuff anywhere but with me.


01:10:37.092 --> 01:10:38.684
You die, Nick.


01:10:39.861 --> 01:10:42.056
You all die.


01:11:09.524 --> 01:11:11.389
You need the medicine
that Carver has.


01:11:13.728 --> 01:11:15.787
I'm not gonna watch you die.


01:11:20.135 --> 01:11:21.864
I'll come back for you.


01:11:28.143 --> 01:11:29.508
I promise.


01:11:43.525 --> 01:11:44.890
When do I open it?


01:11:47.128 --> 01:11:48.925
When you start to
doubt the truth.


01:12:08.550 --> 01:12:10.984
- You know when to open these.
- You sure this is right?


01:12:12.053 --> 01:12:13.418
No.


01:12:20.962 --> 01:12:22.054
Nick?


01:12:24.499 --> 01:12:25.864
Take an umbrella.


01:12:26.735 --> 01:12:28.168
It's gonna rain.


01:12:29.871 --> 01:12:31.702
You be careful, too.


01:12:56.030 --> 01:12:58.430
You make us chase you
halfway across the world...


01:12:58.533 --> 01:13:01.559
then you let a hack like
Pinky Stein bring you in?


01:13:01.703 --> 01:13:04.069
- I'm sick.
- You're sick?


01:13:04.305 --> 01:13:05.772
You don't know what you are.


01:13:08.743 --> 01:13:10.108
Victor, pay the man.


01:13:30.899 --> 01:13:32.230
Of course.


01:13:40.208 --> 01:13:41.971
I knew I wouldn't
get paid yet.


01:13:42.143 --> 01:13:43.405
Wait here.


01:13:44.546 --> 01:13:45.740
Were you followed?


01:13:46.214 --> 01:13:47.738
I'm never followed.


01:13:49.651 --> 01:13:50.913
Where is this guy?


01:13:51.453 --> 01:13:53.011
- Which one?
- The yellow one.


01:13:53.121 --> 01:13:54.611
- The big one?
- Yep.


01:14:26.788 --> 01:14:28.085
Wo Chiang?


01:14:31.726 --> 01:14:33.216
You are here about the girl?


01:14:33.328 --> 01:14:34.886
You're the one
that wiped Kira?


01:14:35.530 --> 01:14:39.762
12 years ago, a woman told me
an American girl would come.


01:14:39.968 --> 01:14:42.732
That was two days
ago, Kira showed.


01:14:44.672 --> 01:14:45.866
I have a job for you.


01:14:49.544 --> 01:14:51.409
Two hours ago, I
wrote seven letters.


01:14:51.546 --> 01:14:53.707
I need you to erase the memory
of ever having written them.


01:14:56.417 --> 01:14:59.045
Seven letters, two
hours of memory.


01:15:00.722 --> 01:15:02.849
The woman tell
me those things.


01:15:04.459 --> 01:15:06.290
She did not pay for you, too.


01:15:10.732 --> 01:15:12.859
And when you're done, I need
you to open this and read it.


01:15:15.770 --> 01:15:16.737
7:34


01:15:17.171 --> 01:15:19.469
- I need a minute.
- As you wish.


01:15:27.815 --> 01:15:31.615
I'm not gonna wake up
and forget who I am, am I?


01:15:38.259 --> 01:15:39.920
7:34... 7:35


01:15:56.411 --> 01:15:59.312
Wait, wait. No, just... go.


01:16:24.872 --> 01:16:26.237
It's all gone.


01:16:27.342 --> 01:16:30.470
The future has... disappeared.


01:16:30.712 --> 01:16:32.077
I lost the connection.


01:16:50.965 --> 01:16:53.490
Halt. Identification?


01:16:54.102 --> 01:16:55.831
Safety inspector...


01:16:57.672 --> 01:16:59.970
I need to know where
the security lockers are.


01:17:00.108 --> 01:17:01.973
Certainly, sir. Go
up the elevator...


01:17:02.343 --> 01:17:04.106
to the top floor.


01:17:04.245 --> 01:17:06.440
- Up this way?
- Yes, sir.


01:17:50.258 --> 01:17:52.021
No problem.


01:18:05.206 --> 01:18:06.867
4,100


01:18:26.627 --> 01:18:28.060
The job is over.


01:18:28.129 --> 01:18:29.687
You don't have to shadow
the building anymore.


01:18:29.831 --> 01:18:31.526
The girl sent me...


01:18:35.103 --> 01:18:36.570
"4,100"


01:18:52.420 --> 01:18:53.853
Thank you.


01:18:54.088 --> 01:18:55.350
You ready?


01:18:58.593 --> 01:19:00.288
Right size, right shape.


01:19:00.728 --> 01:19:02.093
No problem.


01:19:02.897 --> 01:19:04.831
Better hurry. Won't last long.


01:19:25.286 --> 01:19:26.583
Crap.


01:20:25.646 --> 01:20:26.977
The Lord giveth.


01:20:33.254 --> 01:20:36.485
Did you really think you could
slip out of town with this?


01:20:47.268 --> 01:20:49.759
Tell me, was this
worth dying for?


01:21:08.122 --> 01:21:10.488
No. He dies slowly.


01:21:10.591 --> 01:21:14.322
Your sister promised me that
and a great deal of money.


01:21:28.743 --> 01:21:31.769
Do you know how many people in
the world would kill for this drug?


01:21:35.616 --> 01:21:36.640
Now...


01:21:43.224 --> 01:21:44.691
Where is Cassie?


01:21:48.629 --> 01:21:50.460
Get me back on my feet.


01:22:09.250 --> 01:22:11.150
Perhaps the Pop family
can't be relied upon.


01:22:21.963 --> 01:22:23.988
Didn't see that
one coming, did you?


01:22:24.098 --> 01:22:26.623
Do you really want to
do this, little girl?


01:22:26.734 --> 01:22:28.326
I know where the drug is.


01:22:28.402 --> 01:22:31.428
More importantly,
I know how you die.


01:22:31.539 --> 01:22:33.666
Do you want to know
what the tiger means?


01:22:40.548 --> 01:22:41.913
The drug is here.


01:22:42.016 --> 01:22:43.950
See if that will
make him love you.


01:22:53.928 --> 01:22:55.925
My note says I'm
supposed to tell you...


01:22:55.960 --> 01:22:57.923
the Division has Kira.
216 Batang Street.


01:22:59.166 --> 01:23:02.067
It said a lot on there. Was
everyone's that complicated?


01:23:03.170 --> 01:23:04.637
I knew you could handle it.


01:23:11.012 --> 01:23:13.071
This immuno-suppressant
will save your life


01:23:13.180 --> 01:23:15.444
and allow you to reach
your full potential.


01:23:17.385 --> 01:23:19.945
You're going to be
a better you, Kira.


01:23:24.291 --> 01:23:26.623
You need to accept
this reality.


01:23:28.129 --> 01:23:30.393
We're not trying
to hurt you. Kira.


01:23:30.731 --> 01:23:33.632
Matter of fact, your well
being means everything to us.


01:23:34.135 --> 01:23:35.727
Understand it's not your
fault you're forgetting


01:23:35.803 --> 01:23:37.430
who you are and
running from us.


01:23:37.505 --> 01:23:39.063
The drug has side effects.


01:23:39.140 --> 01:23:41.267
We have no way of
knowing the severity.


01:23:42.109 --> 01:23:45.340
I want you to know that I blame
myself for that, Agent Hollis.


01:23:53.921 --> 01:23:55.616
This isn't real.


01:24:05.332 --> 01:24:07.527
You volunteered, Kira.


01:24:08.202 --> 01:24:09.897
I was against it.


01:24:11.138 --> 01:24:14.266
You were certain you'd be
the one to survive the drug.


01:24:14.508 --> 01:24:18.274
I had to support you.
After all, we were partners.


01:24:20.581 --> 01:24:22.446
Then you panicked.


01:24:25.753 --> 01:24:27.220
Did you think you made
it all the way here...


01:24:27.321 --> 01:24:30.256
and eluded us for so
long without any training?


01:24:31.792 --> 01:24:33.817
That's the Division
in you. Kira.


01:24:35.496 --> 01:24:37.225
Now let me help you remember.


01:24:40.468 --> 01:24:42.163
Let me help you remember.


01:24:53.747 --> 01:24:56.773
I keep trying to draw something
different, but I can't.


01:24:59.153 --> 01:25:00.882
It's something to
do with how I die.


01:25:01.021 --> 01:25:02.045
It's a tiger.


01:25:02.323 --> 01:25:04.223
I'm serious.


01:25:05.926 --> 01:25:08.121
I don't know how I
know, but I just know.


01:25:10.030 --> 01:25:13.193
I know I act like I
don't care sometimes,


01:25:14.135 --> 01:25:16.228
- but I don't want to die.
- Cassie...


01:25:20.908 --> 01:25:22.671
It's not gonna happen, okay?


01:25:23.544 --> 01:25:26.012
Just tell me that I'm a crappy
artist and that I'm wrong.


01:25:26.147 --> 01:25:29.708
You are a crappy artist
and you are wrong.


01:25:29.783 --> 01:25:30.909
Listen to me.


01:25:32.153 --> 01:25:34.246
You've already done more
than enough for everyone.


01:25:34.922 --> 01:25:36.685
The only thing you've got
to worry about right now


01:25:36.790 --> 01:25:39.384
- is keeping yourself safe.
- But how?


01:25:40.761 --> 01:25:41.887
Just start walking.


01:25:42.029 --> 01:25:43.087
Don't even think about
where you're going.


01:25:43.164 --> 01:25:46.292
Just keep moving. And don't make
any decisions any watcher can track.


01:25:47.301 --> 01:25:49.166
And when you come
across someplace safe,


01:25:49.870 --> 01:25:52.703
you hide. Simple as that.


01:25:53.307 --> 01:25:55.502
I don't know how, but I
know this is gonna work out.


01:25:55.709 --> 01:25:58.735
I promise. No need to
be scared. Trust me.


01:26:00.948 --> 01:26:02.415
That's more like it.


01:26:22.469 --> 01:26:23.697
What are you gonna do?


01:26:26.707 --> 01:26:27.901
I can't tell you.


01:29:23.050 --> 01:29:26.019
You make me look like a
fool in front of my family!


01:29:32.426 --> 01:29:33.791
Don't worry.


01:29:41.802 --> 01:29:43.531
You won't remember a thing.


01:29:46.940 --> 01:29:48.805
Your mother's very proud.


01:30:00.387 --> 01:30:03.845
I want to make a deal.
The drug for the girl.


01:30:06.460 --> 01:30:07.859
Okay.


01:30:09.263 --> 01:30:11.663
Dock 4, Man Yuen Street.


01:30:27.548 --> 01:30:29.106
Where is the case, Nick?


01:30:29.249 --> 01:30:30.409
Kira!


01:30:36.190 --> 01:30:37.487
Go ahead.


01:30:40.260 --> 01:30:42.660
Remember that night
under the roller coaster?


01:30:44.932 --> 01:30:47.730
We parked in the rain and got
those little bottles of Jack.


01:30:55.309 --> 01:30:57.709
That was the first time
you told me you loved me.


01:31:01.281 --> 01:31:02.509
He remembers.


01:31:04.885 --> 01:31:06.910
I want to hear it from him.


01:31:09.289 --> 01:31:10.654
I remember.


01:31:13.861 --> 01:31:15.294
It never happened.


01:31:18.332 --> 01:31:20.493
We met for the
first time yesterday.


01:31:22.302 --> 01:31:24.167
You've never been
to Coney Island.


01:31:26.173 --> 01:31:28.164
Nobody's been to Coney Island.


01:31:31.345 --> 01:31:33.074
I used you, Nick.


01:31:35.082 --> 01:31:38.142
And the quicker we find that case,
the quicker I'll let you forget it.


01:31:42.723 --> 01:31:44.486
You might as well.


01:31:48.896 --> 01:31:52.662
My card says you have to
take the drug. Give me Carver.


01:31:52.733 --> 01:31:54.064
It's for you.


01:32:01.708 --> 01:32:03.801
- Hello!
- You want the case,


01:32:04.011 --> 01:32:05.342
you let them live.


01:32:05.546 --> 01:32:07.741
I'll tell you
exactly where it is.


01:32:13.086 --> 01:32:15.145
- Another?
- Sure.


01:32:19.326 --> 01:32:20.884
One for the road.


01:33:12.112 --> 01:33:13.739
Don't feel too bad.


01:33:14.448 --> 01:33:17.417
That push of Kira's has
worked on better men.


01:34:08.769 --> 01:34:10.134
4,100


01:34:33.326 --> 01:34:34.816
Kill him.


01:34:37.130 --> 01:34:38.722
If that's alright with you?


01:34:40.100 --> 01:34:41.567
The case...


01:34:49.743 --> 01:34:51.074
Agent Carver.


01:35:00.721 --> 01:35:02.689
The contents of this
case are the property


01:35:02.823 --> 01:35:04.450
of the United
States government.


01:35:04.524 --> 01:35:07.186
Government? We are the
only government here.


01:35:07.294 --> 01:35:10.730
Be reasonable. There is
no need for anyone to die.


01:35:13.133 --> 01:35:15.727
We're not much for
diplomacy these days.


01:35:25.545 --> 01:35:28.708
Victor! Make me
a way out of here!


01:35:43.363 --> 01:35:44.694
Kira!


01:37:20.627 --> 01:37:21.685
Kira!


01:37:42.415 --> 01:37:43.541
Kira...


01:40:22.942 --> 01:40:26.070
Whoa! I'm impressed.


01:40:26.146 --> 01:40:29.309
The engineers are always
conservative with their projections...


01:40:29.382 --> 01:40:30.349
but this is something else.


01:40:30.450 --> 01:40:33.419
Hey! We are on the
same side. Remember?


01:40:33.620 --> 01:40:35.019
Now why don't
you march the men


01:40:35.088 --> 01:40:37.750
who tried to kill us off this
roof, and we'll call it a day.


01:40:38.925 --> 01:40:42.122
Wait! Kira! Don't do this!


01:40:42.362 --> 01:40:45.297
It's a push. What
Carver told you is a lie.


01:40:45.365 --> 01:40:47.060
I'm sure they make
a card for this.


01:40:52.105 --> 01:40:53.470
Where were we?


01:40:54.340 --> 01:40:56.103
Where were we?


01:41:17.831 --> 01:41:19.389
You don't want to do that.


01:41:20.033 --> 01:41:21.022
Watch me.


01:41:21.201 --> 01:41:23.362
You'd be doing me
a favor if you did.


01:41:23.536 --> 01:41:25.060
What's in that
needle will kill you.


01:41:25.171 --> 01:41:27.639
I went through hundreds
of potentials to find her.


01:41:28.508 --> 01:41:29.907
She's our survival.


01:41:33.847 --> 01:41:34.973
Look at me.


01:41:40.086 --> 01:41:41.348
You know me.


01:41:44.057 --> 01:41:45.422
I know you.


01:41:51.231 --> 01:41:52.596
Look at me...


01:41:54.334 --> 01:41:55.562
Look at me.


01:42:02.542 --> 01:42:03.907
Let him do it.


01:42:53.660 --> 01:42:55.321
What a waste.


01:43:33.967 --> 01:43:35.901
I told you to
bring an umbrella.


01:43:40.740 --> 01:43:42.537
Thought you said
it was gonna rain.


01:43:43.109 --> 01:43:45.304
I also told you I get
things wrong sometimes.


01:43:51.451 --> 01:43:53.544
Maybe it will wash the
crap out of your hair.


01:43:59.692 --> 01:44:01.421
So where's the real case?


01:44:15.241 --> 01:44:16.572
There it is.


01:44:18.511 --> 01:44:22.709
How long do you think your
mother has been planning this?


01:44:24.484 --> 01:44:26.111
Since before I was born.


01:44:29.389 --> 01:44:30.481
This is the key, Nick.


01:44:30.623 --> 01:44:31.988
Division will do
anything to keep


01:44:32.091 --> 01:44:33.888
this from getting
into the wrong hands.


01:44:34.761 --> 01:44:36.490
So we trade your
mom for the drug?


01:44:37.897 --> 01:44:39.592
I'm still working on that one.


01:44:43.870 --> 01:44:46.304
Hey, what was it that
I injected myself with?


01:44:46.773 --> 01:44:48.365
Nine Dragon Soy Sauce.


01:44:49.976 --> 01:44:51.341
That's gross.


01:44:52.745 --> 01:44:53.734
What about Kira?


01:44:53.846 --> 01:44:56.110
You're the watcher.
You tell me.


01:44:56.949 --> 01:44:59.577
Don't worry. We'll see
Miss Trouble soon enough.


01:45:32.685 --> 01:45:34.243
When do I open it?


01:45:34.354 --> 01:45:36.288
When you start to
doubt the truth.


01:46:15.928 --> 01:46:18.396
Put your gun in your mouth.


01:46:20.433 --> 01:46:21.900
Pull the trigger.

